David Harvey. Analytical Chemistry 2.1. Author's textbook, hosted by Chemistry LibreTexts. [Complete book, attribution, and chapter menu](https://chem.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analytical_Chemistry/Analytical_Chemistry_2.1_%28Harvey%29).

Use complete chapters 2–7 for tools, analytical vocabulary, data, standardization, equilibrium, and sampling/preparation as the measurement and advanced-solution work develops. Chapters 8–11 supply the assigned gravimetric, titrimetric, spectroscopic, and electrochemical treatments. Chapter 13 supports kinetic observations; chapters 14–15 support method development and quality assurance. The specialist analytical-chemistry trail will deepen the full subject separately.

This is a named, author-attributed open textbook, not an instruction to ingest the host's broader collection. Preserve the actual book/page licence and separately credited components before adaptation. The old DePauw author-page endpoint was not accessible during checking; the attributed book and contents were accessible on the publication host. Author, available edition, chapter identities, and access checked on 29 October 2026. External reference only.

